  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched on June 15th with Sarah Tan as the lead. The initial budget was $500,000, later adjusted to $550,000, and subsequently approved at $2 million by the executive board. The project has expanded its team with Mike Chen and Lisa Ray, explored a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology, and increased its compliance plan budget to $55,000. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th) and a breakthrough in predictive analytics during Phase Two, with a detailed report scheduled for the November 20th staff meeting."
